<BaseLayout
  title="Terms of service — secure-mcp"
  description="Terms for using secure-mcp: license-gated access, authorized defensive review only, findings as candidates, and no warranty."
  path="/terms/"
>
  <PageIntro
    eyebrow="Terms"
    title="Clear terms for a defensive tool."
    titleId="terms-title"
    lede="Short and factual — what the product is, how it may be used, and what it does not promise."
  />

  <LegalProse>
    <h2>The service</h2>
    <p>
      secure-mcp is a local Model Context Protocol server that helps coding
      agents perform defensive, remediation-focused security review of source
      repositories. It is a proprietary product and is licensed, not sold.
    </p>

    <h2>License and keys</h2>
    <p>
      The server requires a valid license key and refuses to start without
      one. A documented development key is available for local evaluation and
      CI testing only. You are responsible for keeping keys private and for
      using them in line with the license you were granted.
    </p>

    <h2>Authorized use</h2>
    <p>
      Use secure-mcp only on codebases you own or are explicitly authorized to
      review. The product is defensive by mandate: it identifies potential
      weaknesses, classifies them, and recommends remediation. You agree not
      to use it, its output, or its skills to generate exploit or attack code,
      to bypass or weaponize discovered weaknesses, or to misuse discovered
      credentials.
    </p>

    <h2>Findings are candidates</h2>
    <p>
      Findings are evidence-oriented candidates produced by bounded static
      inspection. They are not guarantees, vulnerability declarations, or
      permission to act. Confirm findings in code and understand the runtime
      context before remediating. Coverage reports state what was and was not
      reviewed — read them before relying on an empty result.
    </p>

    <h2>No warranty</h2>
    <p>
      The product is provided “as is” without warranty of any kind, express or
      implied, including fitness for a particular purpose. In no event shall
      the authors be liable for any claim, damages, or other liability arising
      from or in connection with the product or its output.
    </p>

    <h2>Intellectual property</h2>
    <p>
      The product, its source code, documentation, and skills are proprietary
      and all rights are reserved. Nothing in these terms grants you a
      license to the product's source code or the rights to redistribute it.
    </p>

    <h2>Changes</h2>
    <p>
      These terms may be updated from time to time; the version on this page
      always applies to current use.
    </p>

    <h2>Contact</h2>
    <p>
      Questions about these terms? Use the{" "}
      <a href="/support/">support form</a> — it opens an email draft on your
      device and sends nothing until you choose Send.
    </p>
  </LegalProse>
</BaseLayout>
